# Web portal

`apps/web` is one Angular app for the user shell (`/user`) and the CMS shell (`/cms`). Both ship in the same nginx image. nginx only serves the static build (`try_files` to `index.html`). It does not check roles.

Authorization stays in `bff-web` (HU-74/75). Route visibility in the client is not a security boundary.

Views are standalone, `OnPush`, and passive: binding and events only. No HTTP, no domain rules, no literal UI strings. Text comes from `ngx-translate` catalogs (`es-CO` default, plus `es-MX`, `es-CL`, `es-PE`).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — view calls the API
this.http.get('/policies');

// ✅ GOOD — view binds a ViewModel
<section [attr.data-status]="vm.status()">
  <h1>{{ 'shell.user.title' | translate }}</h1>
</section>
```

ViewModels hold presentation state (`idle` | `ready` | later `loading` | `degraded` | `error`). They do not touch `HttpClient`, the router, or the DOM. New screens go under `src/app/features/` as lazy routes.
